      "narration": "Marcus’s older daughter is 24, finished with school, working part time and living in another city. Under the Affordable Care Act she may stay on his plan until she turns 26, regardless of whether she is a student, married, financially dependent or living at home. Maryland law separately requires coverage of unmarried child dependents to age 25; the federal rule governs plans subject to it, and the more generous rule applies. When she reaches 26 she loses eligibility, which is a qualifying event for COBRA or Maryland continuation and a special enrollment opportunity on Maryland Health Connection.",
